there is safety in the shadows for this  young zimbabwean  his name is tawanda mucheowa and he's  been hiding for months  in an unlit corner of a large african  city  there are many times whereby i cry  but you know it's some more at some  moments you feel like you are crying in  the dark  and no one is seeing your tears in july  machiawa was abducted and tortured for  three successive days  it was an ordeal that nearly killed him  now he wants to bring those responsible  to justice  my abduction is one in a thousand  and something must be done to  stop the zimbabwean government  the 22 year old was sitting in a car in  front of this shop  in the city of bulawayo when a group of  men  thought to be members of the security  services seized him  and stuffed him in the back of a pickup  truck  he says he was driven out of town and  tortured  and sexually abused for the following 72  hours  it's an experience that will never leave  him someday you feel like you're not  okay  then the other day you're breaking down  the other day i'm shaking  so you know it's now sort of my life now  it's like a roller coaster it's ups and  downs  so i'm so traumatized i think i can say  human rights lawyers say dozens of  government critics and activists  have been abducted in the last few years  but this  alleged abduction was caught on cctv  the camera even capturing a license  plate belonging to one of the team  members  involved the government they know  exactly who abducted me  they know the perpetrators they know the  people who are involved  they have all the details in black and  white  the vehicle registration on the pickup  was traced to a car rental company  called impala  and activists have called on the firm to  release the name of the person who  rented it  but impala refused  so this group locked the company's staff  in their office in protest  the head of zimbabwe's student union has  also called on impala to release the  information  but he was attacked by unknown  assailants when he attempted to hold a  press conference  muchella has also tried to get the name  obtaining an order from the high court  which instructed impala to provide it  but in this letter the company says the  zimbabwean police  has already taken the relevant files  sharif went there to collect the  documents and impala said  they no longer have the documents you  know it's just so ridiculous  how can a company like impala failed to  have  maybe some backup copies of that  information  you know that your car was used to  commit a crime against humanity  which is a climate international law  sky news has discovered that the man who  runs impala  thompson dondo is a fugitive from  british justice  he ran a nursing agency in the uk but  left the country  after he was charged with immigration  offences  in a statement cleveland police told us  if he attempted to re-enter the uk  he would be placed before the courts in  response  a spokesperson for impala said his court  case dragged on for more than  13 months he legally left the uk as he  had no means to sustain his livelihood  has the abduction radicalized you  three days of being tortured  three days not knowing what is going to  happen to you  people discussing about how they are  going to kill you you know in a way it  really changes your mind  and i think in my case i think it made  me to  see that you know there is nothing to  live for  if you don't have freedom the government  has not commented on claims made by  tawanda macheowa  although it's accused people of faking  such incidents  in return for western funds and they're  proposing legislation  criminalizing those who make allegations  of abductions and torture  but this 22 year old exile will not be  silenced  john sparks sky news
 

